    'datasets':{name:'Published Datasets', svc:null, canonical:'https://theflatratemovers.com/datasets/', desc:'Every dataset The Flat Rate Movers publishes — 32 CC BY 4.0 dataset files with canonical landing pages, node inventories, downloads and signed SHA-256 certificates, plus the estate’s Zenodo DOI for the intent-coverage rubric.'},'when-an-item-needs-a-custom-crate':{name:"When an item needs a custom crate and when padding is enough",svc:'service-crating',canonical:'https://theflatratemovers.com/when-an-item-needs-a-custom-crate/',desc:"The crate-or-padding decision made plain: five triggers that settle it (fragile structure, hand-offs, shape, border, storage), a piece-by-piece decision table, what padding cannot do, third-party cost ranges labeled as context, the ISPM 15 rules that govern an export crate's wood, and how crating is surveyed and quoted at one flat rate from Winchester VA and Martinsburg WV to the Port of Virginia."},'i-81-shenandoah-valley-move-timing':{name:"I-81 through the Shenandoah Valley: what it means for move timing",svc:'service-route81',canonical:'https://theflatratemovers.com/i-81-shenandoah-valley-move-timing/',desc:"What I-81's 325 Virginia miles mean for scheduling a move: the corridor's truck volume and terrain in VDOT's own figures, where the worst delay segments actually concentrate (the northern, Staunton District stretch), the 65-project improvement program running to 2035, a pre-move timing checklist built on VDOT's project list and 511, and why a written flat rate means an incident changes the arrival conversation, not the invoice."},'transloading-vs-cross-docking-vs-deconsolidation':{name:"Transloading vs cross-docking vs deconsolidation in plain terms",svc:'service-transloading',canonical:'https://theflatratemovers.com/transloading-vs-cross-docking-vs-deconsolidation/',desc:"The three dock operations separated by what actually changes: transloading changes the vehicle, cross-docking changes only the door (no storage), deconsolidation changes the shipment itself. With the consolidation arithmetic (three maritime containers into two 53-foot domestic trailers), the Federal Maritime Commission's demurrage and detention definitions, the Virginia Inland Port chain at Front Royal, and how the work is priced \u2014 per job, one flat rate in writing, no per-container schedule."},'moving-an-office-inside-a-plant-or-warehouse':{name:"Moving an office inside a plant or warehouse: access, staging, sequence",svc:'service-industrial-offices',canonical:'https://theflatratemovers.com/moving-an-office-inside-a-plant-or-warehouse/',desc:"Why an office inside a plant or warehouse moves differently from a commercial office: the setting \u2014 dock access, move hours, security sign-in, production adjacency \u2014 changes the plan. Covers the pre-move access check (including OSHA's materials-handling rule, 29 CFR 1910.176, on marked, clear aisles at docks and doorways), phased moves and staging, the published seven-step sequence, the certificate-of-insurance question answered honestly, and named industrial parks around Winchester and Martinsburg."},'1650-lb-gun-safe-delivered-and-installed-moorefield-wv':{name:"A 1,650 lb gun safe, delivered and installed in a Moorefield basement",svc:'service-gun-safe',canonical:'https://theflatratemovers.com/1650-lb-gun-safe-delivered-and-installed-moorefield-wv/',desc:"A job story with the crew's own photographs: a 1,650 lb Winchester Big Daddy XLT2 gun safe delivered and installed in a Moorefield, WV basement on October 29, 2026 \u2014 staged on its shipping skid, crossed over gravel on a six-wheel all-terrain dolly, blanket-wrapped through the basement-level double doors, placed, unwrapped, and the crate and packaging removed. Told inside the company's published gun-safe practice: SIR and the KIM-GS Protocol for the 1,500 to 3,500 lb band, safes emptied first, equipment matched to the project, re-anchoring on request, one flat rate in writing."},
